Respect XNN_ENABLE_ASSEMBLY when selecting x86 GEMM kernels.

CMake omits the assembly sources when this option is disabled. Guard the
FP32, BF16 and AVX512VNNI kernel registrations accordingly. Use the existing
intrinsics fallbacks for FP32 and AVX512VNNI.

The BF16 implementation in this snapshot has no intrinsics fallback.
Disabling assembly leaves bf16_f32_gemm_config zero-initialized even on
CPUs supporting BF16. Check mr, the microkernel's row tile size: mr == 0
means no kernel was selected. Return NULL in that case so operator creation
reports xnn_status_unsupported_hardware. This follows the existing PF32
configuration initializer.

